{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgzCKAcnUHaWBuqiyTu4D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`KILN_LEGACY_TZ=1` is a backward-compatibility switch in `kiln/timeparse.py:3-13`. When it's set, `parse()` reads timestamps that have no timezone as UTC, the way kiln worked before 2.0. Without it, they're read as local time.\n\nIt does look unnecessary for the test step:\n- **The tests don't depend on it.** I ran `python3 -m unittest` without it and all 3 tests still pass. The test that uses a timestamp with no timezone (`tests/test_timeparse.py:10`) only checks `.hour == 8`. That's 8 whether the timestamp is read as UTC or local time, because attaching a timezone doesn't shift the clock time.\n- **Nothing records why it's there.** It arrived with the initial commit `d274cef`, and no commit message or comment explains putting it in SETUP.md.\n\nTwo caveats before you remove it:\n- **The switch itself is still live code.** Only its use in SETUP.md looks stale. If anyone runs kiln with pre-2.0 data, they may still need it.\n- **My test check was limited.** It ran on one machine and one timezone. With the current tests that shouldn't matter. But if someone wanted the tests to run in \"legacy mode\" on purpose, for a test that's planned or kept elsewhere, that reason isn't written down anywhere I can find.\n\nIf you want, I can drop it from step 4. That could go in the same commit as the step 2 `--db-url` fix."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":213,"cache_read_input_tokens":21168,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":213},"output_tokens":490,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-52>","timestamp":"2026-11-13T03:12:13.332Z","request_id":"req_011CgzCKASd7LyC3wnRxhJ2u"}
